review:
I try my best to judge a game based on the game itself, but, as one can see from the other posted reviews, it's not always possible to ignore outside factors about a game like the game's management and administration. I shall read the poem "First They Came" by Martin Niemöller as my first and final Poetry Jam reading to best explain my point:

"When the Nazis came for the communists,
I kept quiet; I wasn't a communist.
When they came for the trade unionists, I kept quiet;
I wasn't a trade unionist.
When they locked up the social democrats, I kept quiet;
I wasn't a social democrat.
When they locked up the Jews, I kept quiet;
I wasn't a Jew.
When they came for me, there was no one left to protest."
